   7:     """Move each red vertical bar upward in its column until it rests directly under the blue pixels above it.
   8: 
   9:     Input structure
  10:     - The grid has a black background, an upper blue shape, and lower red vertical bars.
  11:     - Every column containing red has one contiguous red segment below at least one blue pixel.
  12: 
  13:     Rule
  14:     - Clear the red cells from their starting positions.
  15:     - In each red column, preserve the red segment height and repaint it starting one row below the lowest blue pixel in that same column.
  16: 
  17:     Key insight
  18:     - Each red bar slides straight upward along its own column; the blue pixels in that column define the stopping position.
  19:     """
